orks (2018: 6, 2022: 9, 2023: 8), too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2019–2021 have a median of 0–5.5 citations each; the highest median (5.5) is in 2020.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2020 have at least 19.6 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2021–2026 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 3 of 3 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2020: mean 8.9, median 5.5, top work 26. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2026 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2019–2021 and 2024–2026 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2018 and 2022–2023 have fewer than 10 works (2018: 6, 2022: 9, 2023: 8), too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}